{"causes": ["The 13th-century rediscovery and translation of Aristotle's complete works into Latin spurred intense philosophical and theological debate across European universities.", "The establishment of the Franciscan Order provided a new intellectual avenue for scholars dedicated to poverty and learning, fostering a dynamic academic environment.", "The burgeoning university system in Oxford and Paris created a competitive intellectual arena where new ideas and interpretations were rigorously discussed and critiqued."], "effects": ["Richard Rufus's philosophical inquiries contributed to the development of early scholastic epistemological theories, particularly regarding the nature of universals and knowledge acquisition.", "His critical engagement with Augustinian thought influenced subsequent Oxford Franciscan theologians, preparing the intellectual ground for figures like Roger Bacon and Duns Scotus.", "His commentaries on Aristotle's *Metaphysics* provided some of the earliest systematic analyses of Aristotelian philosophy within the Western Christian tradition."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "aristotle", "sourceName": "Aristotle", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "richard-rufus-of-cornwall", "targetName": "Richard Rufus of Cornwall", "context": "Aristotle's newly rediscovered philosophical works, particularly the *Metaphysics*, profoundly influenced Richard Rufus's intellectual development and scholarly output around the mid-13th century."}, {"sourceSlug": "richard-rufus-of-cornwall", "sourceName": "Richard Rufus of Cornwall", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "roger-bacon", "targetName": "Roger Bacon", "context": "Richard Rufus's pioneering work in integrating Aristotelian philosophy and his critical epistemology subtly influenced later Oxford Franciscan thinkers, including Roger Bacon, in the mid-13th century."}, {"sourceSlug": "richard-rufus-of-cornwall", "sourceName": "Richard Rufus of Cornwall", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "university-of